+## SMetric
+
+In regular routing mode, `smetric` keeps a continuation on the worker with the longest observed prompt
+prefix while that worker remains within its gate. When the gate rejects the
+home worker, it uses a native Dynamo-style score over all healthy workers.
+
+The policy is self-contained in Router. Its inputs are the approximate prefix
+tree, request start/first-response/completion events, and the resulting
+router-owned in-flight work ledger. It does not read Redis or worker-private
+scheduler state.
+
+SMetric is currently rejected in prefill/decode disaggregated mode because that
+path has two worker lifecycles for one request; treating either one as the
+regular-mode ledger would produce invalid load measurements.
+
+The ready-to-use configuration uses the relative overload gate:
+
+```bash
+vllm-router --policy smetric \
+  --worker-urls http://worker1:8000,http://worker2:8000
+```
+
+The work ledger counts uncached prompt units until the first response bytes
+arrive, then counts the request's context units until the response stream ends.
+The default fallback gives the approximate device-prefix match full credit and
+uses zero host-cache credit because Router has no native host-cache signal.
+
+The optional attention-budget gate measures each worker's drain rate online.
+It records queue-free first-response samples in a trailing window and uses the
+cold-start value until enough samples exist:
+
+```bash
+vllm-router --policy smetric \
+  --smetric-gate budget_attention \
+  --smetric-drain-window-secs 300 \
+  --smetric-drain-min-samples 8 \
+  --smetric-drain-tps-fallback 21400 \
+  --worker-urls http://worker1:8000,http://worker2:8000
+```
+
+The main parameters are:
+
+| CLI option | Default | Description |
+|------------|---------|-------------|
+| `--smetric-gate` | `overload` | `overload` or `budget_attention` |
+| `--smetric-overload-factor` | `2.0` | Maximum home load relative to fleet mean |
+| `--smetric-hit-ratio` | `0.5` | Required observed prefix fraction for sticking |
+| `--smetric-overlap-score-credit` | `1.0` | Device-prefix credit in fallback scoring |
+| `--smetric-active-request-weight` | `0.0` | Optional concurrency term in fallback scoring |
+| `--smetric-budget-gamma` | `1.0` | Multiplier on the attention gate budget |
+| `--smetric-drain-window-secs` | `300` | Sliding calibration window |
+| `--smetric-drain-min-samples` | `8` | Samples required before using the measured median |
+| `--smetric-drain-tps-fallback` | `21400` | Cold-start attention work rate |
+| `--smetric-attention-l-eq` | `6923` | Model attention/linear break-even context |
+
+---
+
